  "id": "2026-11-27-agent-spend-enter",
  "problem_type": "Editor gestures and tool receipts lose the identity of the next user action",
  "symptom": "Composition-end Enter and slash with a chip submit unintended actions. Two presses can confirm two offers. A generate call waiting in preflight is folded as streaming. A stale Generate gesture can replay a failed handoff, a hidden quote ages into keyboard eligibility, and a closed card still requests approval during settlement.",
  "direct_cause": "Capture treated keyCode 229 as plain Enter, chip eligibility overrode slash, and an unscoped button ref could activate each new primary. The receipt joined the operation ID to Pi runningTools, which excludes before_tool. Handoff admission compared only the quote, review time started at render, and the user wait ended only at settlement.",
  "class_root": "Neither input dispatch nor tool presentation binds the waiting user action to its actual owner.",
  "affected_population": [
    "Creators using the resident panel in the sidebar, dock or floating shell and the shared panel in the design lab."
  ],
