    "why_not": "The docks and design fixtures mount the shared cards or the whole panel. Single receipts and work history consume the same tool facts. The language resources supply the existing labels. The desktop host owns the actual wait. The card hook reads the quote and each mounted panel consumes the displayed identity. The handover request crosses the existing renderer, IPC and host boundary. The quote projection owns the ledger revision, the shell and document supply visibility, and the run watcher reports close before settlement."
  },
  "generality_proof": "All resident layouts use the same panel. The displayed spend quoteId covers the project, operation, presentation and shot revisions independently of handoff progress. Lane approvals use the pending toolCallId. The gate publishes all active holds by call ID so concurrent calls and old calls on the same plan keep their own statuses. All handoffs append synchronously to the presentation before dispatch. Its append count and the quote identify the next attempt across windows and reloads. The review clock follows the visible primary button in each layout.",
